{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For the same fate.</b> This verse concerns the thoughts of men who are not wise and discerning, for when they see that there is one fate for man and beast, in life and in death, they think that there is one spirit for all, and man has no advantage over beast. And מותר is on the pattern of מושב, from the heavy stem [binyan], and the heh is a substitute for the root letter yod. And יתרון is from the light stem [binyan], and the nun is added."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:23.309569549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}